<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/athens" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athens.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-19">19 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">First Boston Marathon is run</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715">Fifteen</a> runners set out on the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> race, inspired by the marathon at the 1896 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> Olympics. It is now the world's oldest annual marathon.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/benin-expedition-of-1897">Benin Expedition of 1897</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Benin Expedition of 1897 was a British punitive military campaign against the Benin Empire, launched after the killing of a British party attempting to reach Benin City.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1897" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1897.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1897">Greco-Turkish War (1897)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Greco-Turkish War of 1897, also called the Thirty Days' War, was fought between Greece and the Ottoman Empire over Crete, where Christians had risen against Ottoman rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-zionist-congress" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-zionist-congress.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-zionist-congress">First Zionist Congress</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The First Zionist Congress was the inaugural congress of the Zionist Organization, held in the Stadtcasino in Basel on August 29–31, 1897.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-biak-na-bato" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pact-of-biak-na-bato.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-biak-na-bato">Pact of Biak-na-Bato</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Pact of Biak-na-Bato was a truce agreed in December 1897 between the Spanish governor-general Fernando Primo de Rivera and Emilio Aguinaldo's revolutionaries, mediated by Pedro Paterno.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tejeros-convention" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tejeros-convention.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/tejeros-convention">Tejeros Convention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Tejeros Convention was a meeting of Filipino revolutionaries held at Tejeros in Cavite on 22 March 1897 to settle the rivalry between the Magdalo and Magdiwang factions of the Katipunan.</p></div></li></ol></section>
